Avoid the reserved word `transient` in a var declaration.

Qt 6.8's QML parser still treats `transient` as a future reserved word, so
`var transient = false` fails to parse and takes the whole notifications
service down with "Expected token `identifier'". Newer Qt, which upstream
Quickshell builds against, parses it fine. The rename is local to the
function and changes no behaviour.

--- a/shell/plugins/notifications/Service.qml
+++ b/shell/plugins/notifications/Service.qml
@@
-    var transient = false
+    var isTransient = false
     try {
-      transient = !!(notification.hints && notification.hints["transient"])
-    } catch (e) { transient = false }
+      isTransient = !!(notification.hints && notification.hints["transient"])
+    } catch (e) { isTransient = false }
